{# CI/CD integration — a modal opened from the component header ⋮ menu (open-cicd window event), not a body card. #}
{% comment %}
One command, not a configurator.

This used to ask which of five CI platforms you were on, which of three SBOM
sources you had, and whether you wanted augment / enrich / save-to-file, then
render the YAML those answers produced. Every one of those questions is one the
wizard asks in the repository it is being run in, where it can look and answer
most of them itself.

The command is written out in the markup rather than assembled in JavaScript.
Only the token varies, so it is one span; building the whole string in an
x-data attribute meant escaping shell quotes and newlines through an HTML
attribute, and djlint collapses that attribute onto one line, which turns any
// comment in it into a comment over the rest of the code.

That span is also why the block is not c-code-block: that component takes its
code as a prop, because whitespace inside a pre element is content, and a prop
cannot carry a bound span. The block keeps the two stylesheet classes it always
had.

The token is minted on click, not on open. Rendering this dialog is not a
decision to create a credential, and someone opening it three times to read the
command should not leave three live tokens behind.
{% endcomment %}
{% comment %}
Resolved here rather than passed in by each view: two templates include this
dialog, and a context key one of them forgot would break the button silently.
The ``as`` form swallows NoReverseMatch, so a session without a workspace
leaves it empty and the button is not offered rather than 500ing the page.
{% endcomment %}
{% url 'teams:ci_token' team_key=request.session.current_team.key as ci_token_url %}
{# Reachable from onboarding, where there is no component, so the copy
   target needs an id that still resolves. #}
{% firstof component.id 'onboarding' as cicd_copy_suffix %}
<div x-data="{ cicdOpen: false }"
     @open-cicd.window="cicdOpen = true"
     @keydown.escape.window="if (cicdOpen) cicdOpen = false">
    <c-modal show="cicdOpen" title="Get started" icon="fas fa-rocket" x-data="ciCdToken('{{ ci_token_url|escapejs }}')">
    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted mt-0 mb-4">
        Run this in your repository. The wizard detects your CI platform and package
        manager, then writes the pipeline configuration for you.
    </p>
    <div class="tw-code-block">
        <div class="tw-code-block-content">
            <pre><code id="ci-cd-command-{{ cicd_copy_suffix }}">docker run --rm -it \
  -v "$(pwd):/github/workspace" \
  -w /github/workspace \
  -e SBOMIFY_TOKEN=<span x-text="token || '$SBOMIFY_TOKEN'">$SBOMIFY_TOKEN</span> \
  ghcr.io/sbomify/sbomify-action \
  sbomify-action wizard</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="absolute top-2 right-2">
            {% include "core/components/copyable_value.html.j2" with copy_from="ci-cd-command-"|add:cicd_copy_suffix title="Copy command" hide_value=True %}
        </div>
    </div>
    {# Before minting: the command reads an env var the reader may already have. #}
    <div x-show="!token" class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
        {% if not ci_token_url %}
            <span class="text-xs text-text-muted">Set <c-code-inline>SBOMIFY_TOKEN</c-code-inline> to a token from Settings → API tokens.</span>
        {% endif %}
        {% if ci_token_url %}
            <c-buttons.secondary size="sm" @click="mint()" ::disabled="minting" data-testid="mint-ci-token">
            <span x-show="!minting"><i class="fas fa-key mr-2"></i>Add a 7-day token</span>
            <span x-show="minting" x-cloak>Creating…</span>
            </c-buttons.secondary>
            <span class="text-xs text-text-muted">Or set <c-code-inline>SBOMIFY_TOKEN</c-code-inline> yourself.</span>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
    {# After minting: say what it can do and when it stops, because it is now on screen. #}
    <c-feedback.alert variant="info" icon="fas fa-key" class="mt-4" x-show="token" x-cloak>
    Expires <span x-text="expiresAt" class="font-medium"></span>. It can upload artifacts
    and tag releases, nothing else. Revoke it any time in Settings → API tokens.
    </c-feedback.alert>
    <p x-show="error"
       x-cloak
       x-text="error"
       class="text-xs text-danger mt-3 mb-0"></p>
    <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-3 mb-0">For a manual one-off, use Upload artifact in the component menu.</p>
    </c-modal>
</div>
